    "introduction": "Barratt Redrow builds homes in the UK under brands including Barratt Homes, David Wilson Homes and Redrow. The business buys land, obtains planning permission, develops infrastructure and constructs properties for private buyers and housing partners. Revenue is primarily recognised through home sales, making completions, selling prices and construction costs important to results. Its different brands serve a range of buyers and locations, while national scale supports purchasing and development capacity. The business requires capital to be committed to land and construction before homes are sold. Mortgage affordability, planning constraints, build quality and the pace of customer reservations therefore influence both profitability and cash flow.",
